Id: lin038w
Severity: WARN
Category: packages
Check: pkg_integrity
Fix: rpm --setperms PACKAGE, apk fix PACKAGE, or pacman -S PACKAGE.
References: rpm(8); apk(8); pacman(8)
Controls: CIS 2.3; NIST SI-7; ISO 8.19

A file installed by a package has a different mode or owner than the
package set. The check asks the package manager (rpm -V, apk audit,
pacman -Qk), so it covers RPM, Alpine and Arch systems. It is not
reported on Debian or Ubuntu: dpkg records no mode or owner for the files
it installs (dpkg --verify checks md5 sums only), so the dpkg checks
compare content only, and the modes dpkg does record, its overrides, are
lin039w. A binary that has become world-writable, or
changed owner, can be replaced by whoever it now belongs to. Restore it
with the package manager's own tool (rpm --setperms PACKAGE, apk fix
PACKAGE, pacman -S PACKAGE) or, if the change is intended, accept the
finding with tigris-accept.
